WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.790
A weekly content system, AI with a human check, and safe images.

2
00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:10.490
This is the video for module 4 of Content Creation with Canva and Phone Tools.

3
00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:22.920
Most small businesses post when they remember, then go quiet for weeks, and customers forget them. A content system turns this into a weekly routine of about two to three hours.

4
00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:28.180
AI tools can give you fast first drafts, but you stay the editor.

5
00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:32.200
The best light for photos is free: daylight.

6
00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:39.130
And one strong piece of content can become many, using only images you are allowed to use.

7
00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:52.130
Step one. Choose three to five content pillars, the themes you post about again and again. For a bakery: products and offers, tips, behind the scenes, happy customers, and community.

8
00:00:53.380 --> 00:01:00.720
Step two. Be realistic. Three feed posts or Reels a week, plus daily WhatsApp Status, is a sensible start.

9
00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:11.270
Step three. Plan a weekly calendar in a notebook or a Google Sheet. Note market days, salary week, Sallah, Easter and Christmas a month ahead.

10
00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:23.170
Step four. Batch. Shoot all your photos in one daylight session, and design all your posts in one Canva session with your master templates. You set up only once.

11
00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:31.290
Step five. Spend ten minutes a week recording reach, saves, messages and sales. Make more of what works.

12
00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:44.120
For example, Fatima, a tailor in Ilorin, spends about three hours a week. Her sheet showed that her measuring tip brought appointment requests, so she now plans one tip every week.

13
00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:55.460
Generative AI creates text or images from your instructions, called prompts. A weak prompt like, write a caption for my cake, gives a generic answer.

14
00:01:56.710 --> 00:02:13.310
A strong prompt has five parts: who you are, the audience, what you want, the format, and the tone. For example: I run a home bakery in Ibadan. Write three captions under 50 words for a red velvet cake, for mothers planning parties. Warm and simple.

15
00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:23.070
Here is a worked example. Folake writes a strong prompt for three bags, for women going to owambe parties, ending with WhatsApp to order.

16
00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:35.610
She gives the AI her real prices: about 15,000, 18,500 and 22,000 naira. It returns nine captions, and she picks three.

17
00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:47.740
Then the human check. One caption said the bags were waterproof. They are not, so she deletes it. She rewrites each in her own words, with a Yoruba greeting she really uses.

18
00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:51.690
Three captions in about 15 minutes, with no false claims.

19
00:02:52.940 --> 00:03:01.070
AI can state things that sound confident but are false. This is often called hallucination. Check every fact yourself.

20
00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:10.470
Use real photos for products. If customers buy because of an AI picture, they will be disappointed and may report you.

21
00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:23.480
Never paste private customer data into AI tools. And beware of apps promising AI that will make you rich for an upfront fee. Never share your social media passwords with them.

22
00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:31.210
Place your product beside a window, with light from the side. Cover direct sun with a thin white curtain.

23
00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:36.980
Hold a sheet of white cardboard on the opposite side to lift dark shadows.

24
00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:42.520
Avoid the flash. It flattens the subject and causes harsh shadows.

25
00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:50.450
Turn on gridlines and place the product on a third line. Clean the background, and walk closer instead of zooming.

26
00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:57.760
Edit lightly. If a fabric looks different from your photo when it arrives, you lose the customer's trust.

27
00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:15.970
One rich video can become a Reel, Status clips, a carousel, a quote graphic and a caption. For the pictures, use your own photos, Canva's free items, Unsplash or Pexels. With Creative Commons, give credit, and avoid NC, which means no business use.

28
00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:28.080
A photo on Google or someone's Instagram is not free just because you can download it. In Nigeria, copyright falls under the Copyright Act 2022.

29
00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:30.070
When in doubt, leave it out.

30
00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:43.200
To remember. Pillars, a steady pace and batching. AI drafts, you decide. Side window light, no flash. One core piece, many formats. And only images you are allowed to use.

31
00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:56.820
Your turn. Plan and batch one week of content. Draft captions with AI, then check and rewrite them. Shoot a product set with window light. And repurpose one video into four formats.

32
00:04:57.170 --> 00:04:59.120
Continue with the lessons below.
